Fix rules-eval.md bug B2 (-p has no effect) for the istree golden harness.

NOT a reference-build patch: it lives in a subdirectory so that
reference/build.sh (which applies reference/patches/*.patch) never picks
it up. reference/harness/istree/gen.sh applies it to an out-of-tree copy.

1. fpg_mine: call ist_seteval before ist_filter (upstream filters with the
   ist_create defaults, eval = RE_NONE, so nothing but infrequent sets is
   marked), and call ist_filter for every prune > ITEM_MIN (a positive
   value selects the strong forward filter branch, which upstream only
   reaches from apriori).
2. ist_clomax (generators): compare the single items with the total
   weight without the skip flag; with (1), ist_filter marks the empty set
   and the flagged (negative) weight made every item a non-generator.

